.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rars 1 "" rars
.SH NAME
rars \- Pure\-Rust RAR archive toolkit
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrars\fR [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
rars reads, writes, and repairs RAR archives across the RAR 1.3 through RAR 7.x family.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR
Worker threads for parallel compression and extraction (default: all available cores)
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<PROGRESS>\fR [default: auto]
Progress reporting mode for long\-running operations
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
rars\-info(1)
Display archive metadata
.TP
rars\-test(1)
Verify archive integrity by extracting to a sink
.TP
rars\-extract(1)
Extract archive contents
.TP
rars\-repair(1)
Repair a damaged archive using its recovery record
.TP
rars\-add(1)
Create a new archive
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Exit codes:
  0  success
  1  operation failed
  2  invalid command line
  3  password required, wrong password, or corrupt encrypted data
